2:T5a9,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a fitted kitchen cost in the UK on average?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough UK guide, a typical mid-range fitted kitchen may cost around £12,000–£20,000 including units, worktops, appliances and installation. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to fit a kitchen without buying the units?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough UK guide, straightforward installation may typically cost around £2,000–£5,000, but plumbing, electrical work, tiling, flooring, removal and worktop fitting can increase the total. Every project differs, so get a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to buy a kitchen from a retailer or use a local fitter?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Neither option is always cheaper. Compare complete, itemised quotes and check whether design, delivery, fitting, connections, waste disposal and finishing work are included."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the most effective way to save money on a new kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping the existing layout can reduce plumbing, electrical and flooring changes. Standard units and mid-range worktops can also help control costs."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-does-a-fitted-kitchen-cost-uk","d"]
